Training has not started: the check that must pass before any training missed one of its three bars by 0.3 point, so the campaign stopped and is waiting for your decision.

## What the check measured
Before any training, the law re-reads three known numbers on 100 dense document pages. The metric is "page word recall": the share of a page's words the model can rebuild from its compressed slots. Higher is better.

| check | today | recorded | bar | result |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| recorded stage-2 model (the start of every arm), recall ↑ | .715 | .702 | .702 ± .01 | missed by .003 |
| model trained on these 100 pages (known positive), recall ↑ | .921 | .921 | .921 ± .01 | pass, all 100 rebuilt texts identical |
| reference transcription paired with itself | 1.000 | 1.000 | 1.000 | pass |

## Why the miss is noise, not a code change
- **Code unchanged:** the only edit to `pisco/model.py` since the recorded run is a switch that is off by default and off here.
- **Same output on one node:** on homer-019, today's code wrote the recorded text exactly for the first 5 pages.
- **Different output on another:** on homer-017 (same A100 model), the full 100-page pass changed 99 of 100 rebuilt texts.
- **No real difference overall:** today minus recorded is +1.3 points (95% interval −2.4 to +5.2; p .54).
- **Large swings per page:** 28 of 100 pages move by more than 10 points between two reads of the same model.
- **Why only this model moves:** the rebuild is long (768 tokens, always taking the top token), and this model is unsure, so a tiny rounding difference sends it down another path. The model trained on these pages is very sure, so it does not move.
- **Not proven:** what makes the two nodes differ. My guess, untested, is the kernel settings that Qwen3.5's linear-attention layers choose by timing.

**Consequence for later:** this noise alone gives about ±4 points of uncertainty on a 100-page set. The first gate (gate 1, page word recall after the stage-2 trainings) needs a +3-point gain, so on the 100-page sets only large gains will show. The 360 eval pages (about ±2 points) will decide it.

## Done this wake
- Closed the three check jobs and recorded their numbers and the diagnosis.
- Wrote the results page `docs/stage2_rebuild.md` and the question in `campaign_rebuild/BLOCKED.md`.
- Spent about 2.4 of 190 GPU-hours. Nothing new was launched.

**Cost warning:** recall takes 23 s per page, not the 14 s the plan assumed. Gate 1 recall now projects to about 21 GPU-hours instead of 12, so about 200 of 190 in total. The loop will ask you before it goes over.

**Your decision:** I recommend **A**. It costs nothing now and keeps every gate's bar. It loosens the ±1-point bar on this check, so it needs your word.
- **A (recommended):** count the check as passed. The next wake starts the four short stage-2 test runs: about 2 GPU-hours, then about 120 for the full runs. At gate 1, each page set is read in one job on one node, with a fresh read of the old stage-2 model beside the control. That adds about 1.3 GPU-hours.
- **B:** first measure the noise on more nodes (about 2 GPU-hours), then I ask again.
- **C:** stop the campaign.
